## Anaemia 85
- Anaemia in CKD is related to:
- reduced erythropoietin production by the kidney;
- resistance to the action of erythropoiesis stimulating agents (ESA);
- reduced absorption of iron.
- Anaemia related to CKD usually starts to develop when the GFR is less than 60 mL/min/1.73m 2 . The prevalence of anaemia increases with decreasing GFR.
